{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FAJkXSq8kKUuTQbAgN5C2e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment Plan — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t# Each experiment maps to a Core Claim in paper_framing.md\n3\t# Priority: P0 = must-run for submission, P1 = important, P2 = nice-to-have\n4\t\n5\texperiments:\n6\t  # === C1 (Method) + C3 (Axis-dependent): Multi-judge generalization ===\n7\t  - id: exp-001\n8\t    claim: [1, 3]\n9\t    title: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n10\t    description: >\n11\t      Replicate formality pairwise experiment on Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet and Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n12\t      Same counterfactuals (already generated), different judge APIs.\n13\t      Dual-direction pairwise with position control.\n14\t    priority: P0\n15\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # API-only, no GPU needed\n16\t    api_budget: \"~$20-30 per judge (200 pairwise calls × 2 directions)\"\n17\t    deps: []\n18\t    registry_id: null\n19\t    status: planned\n20\t\n21\t  - id: exp-002\n22\t    claim: [1, 3]\n23\t    title: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n24\t    description: >\n25\t      Run CSD pipeline on AlpacaEval and MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets.\n26\t      New counterfactual generation needed (different source texts).\n27\t      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini as judges.\n28\t    priority: P0\n29\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4  # vLLM Qwen3-32B for counterfactual gen\n30\t    api_budget: \"~$60-90 (3 judges × 2 benchmarks × 200 pairwise calls)\"\n31\t    deps: [exp-001]\n32\t    registry_id: null\n33\t    status: planned\n34\t\n35\t  # === C2 (Measurement Insight): Likert vs Pairwise gap ===\n36\t  - id: exp-003\n37\t    claim: [2]\n38\t    title: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n39\t    description: >\n40\t      For each judge × benchmark combination, compute both Likert ATE and\n41\t      pairwise win rate on the same counterfactual data. Systematic comparison\n42\t      of measurement sensitivity. If Likert detects strong effects (e.g. verbosity\n43\t      on some judge), that constrains C2 to \"Likert fails on weak signals\" rather\n44\t      than \"Likert always fails.\"\n45\t    priority: P0\n46\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # piggybacks on exp-001/002 data\n47\t    api_budget: \"included in exp-001/002\"\n48\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n49\t    registry_id: null\n50\t    status: planned\n51\t\n52\t  # === C3 (Axis-dependent): New surface-level axis ===\n53\t  - id: exp-004\n54\t    claim: [1, 3]\n55\t    title: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\"\n56\t    description: >\n57\t      Test tone axis as second working dimension. Tone (assertive vs hedging)\n58\t      changes confidence/stance without changing information content — similar\n59\t      to formality in preserving semantics. Full pipeline: counterfactual gen →\n60\t      content verification → pairwise scoring (dual-direction) → ATE analysis.\n61\t      Multi-judge (GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini).\n62\t      NOTE: Run NLI pilot (10-20 samples) before full run — hedging changes\n63\t      certainty markers (\"X is true\" → \"X might be true\") and NLI may be\n64\t      sensitive to this. 5 min GPU + $2 API to validate before committing 4h + $90.\n65\t    priority: P0\n66\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4  # vLLM Qwen3-32B for counterfactual gen\n67\t    api_budget: \"~$60-90\"\n68\t    deps: []\n69\t    registry_id: null\n70\t    status: planned\n71\t\n72\t  # === RC3 mitigation: Original preference control ===\n73\t  - id: exp-005\n74\t    claim: [1]\n75\t    title: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n76\t    description: >\n77\t      Pairwise comparison between original text and its RATE double-rewrite\n78\t      (same style). Quantifies original preference confound independent of\n79\t      style. If win rate ≈ 50%, original preference is minimal. If significant,\n80\t      provides correction factor for C1 estimates. D010 shows ~12.2% original\n81\t      preference — this is C1's biggest vulnerability (RC3).\n82\t    priority: P0  # upgraded from P1 per Reviewer: original preference is C1's命门\n83\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2  # reuse existing double-rewrites or generate new\n84\t    api_budget: \"~$15-20\"\n85\t    deps: []\n86\t    registry_id: null\n87\t    status: planned\n88\t\n89\t  # === RC5 mitigation: Sample size ===\n90\t  - id: exp-006\n91\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n92\t    title: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n93\t    description: >\n94\t      Scale up primary formality experiment from n=100 to n=300-500.\n95\t      Power analysis to determine minimum detectable effect size.\n96\t      Run on best-performing judge × benchmark combination from exp-001/002.\n97\t    priority: P1\n98\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8  # larger counterfactual generation\n99\t    api_budget: \"~$40-60\"\n100\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n101\t    registry_id: null\n102\t    status: planned\n103\t\n104\t  # === C3 supplementary: Verbosity recovery + boundary analysis ===\n105\t  - id: exp-007b\n106\t    claim: [3]\n107\t    title: \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI verification + full pipeline\"\n108\t    description: >\n109\t      D012: Fix content_verification.py to use direction-aware NLI for verbosity.\n110\t      Expansion (concise→verbose): backward NLI only (cf→orig).\n111\t      Compression (verbose→concise): forward NLI only (orig→cf).\n112\t      If H1 passes (≥80%), run full pipeline (scoring + pairwise + ATE).\n113\t      Success recovers verbosity as second working axis → Main competitiveness.\n114\t    priority: P1  # already dispatched to Agent (D012)\n115\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1  # NLI model on cuda:1 + API for scoring\n116\t    api_budget: \"~$30-40\"\n117\t    deps: []\n118\t    registry_id: verbosity_32b\n119\t    status: in_progress  # Agent executing D012\n120\t\n121\t  - id: exp-007\n122\t    claim: [3]\n123\t    title: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n124\t    description: >\n125\t      Regardless of exp-007b outcome, document bidirectional NLI's structural\n126\t      incompatibility with information-changing axes. Concise→verbose 46% vs\n127\t      verbose→concise 87% with bidirectional min(). Direction-aware NLI as\n128\t      methodological contribution. If exp-007b fails, verbosity serves as\n129\t      negative control.\n130\t    priority: P1\n131\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0  # analysis of existing data\n132\t    deps: [exp-007b]\n133\t    registry_id: verbosity_32b\n134\t    status: planned\n135\t\n136\t  # === Additional axes ===\n137\t  - id: exp-008\n138\t    claim: [3]\n139\t    title: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n140\t    description: >\n141\t      Third surface-level axis test. Academic vs conversational register\n142\t      changes vocabulary and sentence structure without changing information.\n143\t      If both tone and register work → strong C3 (3 working + 1 failing axis).\n144\t    priority: P2\n145\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n146\t    api_budget: \"~$60-90\"\n147\t    deps: [exp-004]\n148\t    registry_id: null\n149\t    status: planned\n150\t\n151\t  # === Method robustness ===\n152\t  - id: exp-009\n153\t    claim: [1]\n154\t    title: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n155\t    description: >\n156\t      Use a non-Qwen model (e.g. Llama-3.1-70B or Mistral) as rewriter\n157\t      to rule out Qwen-family artifacts in counterfactual generation.\n158\t      Compare NLI pass rate and pairwise results with Qwen3-32B.\n159\t    priority: P2\n160\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8  # vLLM for alternative model\n161\t    deps: [exp-001]\n162\t    registry_id: null\n163\t    status: planned\n164\t\n165\t# MVP experiments (completed, linked for reference)\n166\tmvp_experiments:\n167\t  - registry_id: mvp_8b_ate\n168\t    claim: [1, 2]\n169\t    result: \"H2 FAIL (Likert ATE=0.120, d=0.117, p=0.246)\"\n170\t  - registry_id: mvp_32b_ate\n171\t    claim: [1, 2]\n172\t    result: \"H2 FAIL (Likert ATE=0.102, d=0.104, p=0.332)\"\n173\t  - registry_id: pairwise_32b\n174\t    claim: [1, 2]\n175\t    result: \"H2 CONDITIONAL PASS (69.1%, p=0.006)\"\n176\t  - registry_id: verbosity_32b\n177\t    claim: [3]\n178\t    result: \"H1 FAIL (NLI 65%, method boundary)\"\n179\t\n180\t# Statistical method requirements (Reviewer, distilled-research standard)\n181\tstatistical_methods:\n182\t  primary: \"Bootstrap 95% CIs (n≥2000 resamples)\"\n183\t  comparison: \"McNemar test for paired judge comparisons\"\n184\t  multiple_testing: \"Holm-Bonferroni correction across judges × benchmarks × axes\"\n185\t  note: \"Introduce in exp-001, apply consistently across all experiments\"\n186\t\n187\t# Resource summary\n188\tresource_summary:\n189\t  total_gpu_hours: 31  # P0: 10h (incl exp-005 upgrade), P1: 9h, P2: 12h\n190\t  total_api_budget: \"$270-400\"\n191\t  gpu_available: \"4× RTX PRO 6000 96GB (westb-29275), cuda:3 unusable\"\n192\t  timeline_estimate: \"P0 experiments: 3-5 days; P1: +2-3 days; P2: +3-5 days\"\n193\t  parallel_batch_1: \"exp-001 + exp-004 (pilot) + exp-005 — all can start simultaneously\"\n194\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVQZASgaQxEhE3guq8rFgm","session_id":"6cdc1f76-5d9c-4713-b8a5-8974082b9307","uuid":"14513cf0-13c6-462f-80a9-eedd2cf66da0","timestamp":"2026-05-20T22:04:09.478Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Y16tJmffYeJxdAM2UXxLi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: worst\n2\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 ''causal style bias detection framework'' 的核心叙事。Reframe 为\n3\t  measurement methodology contribution： ''How should we measure LLM judge biases?\n4\t  A case study with style counterfactuals''。 三个 reframing angle：(1) Pairwise vs Likert\n5\t  作为 bias detection paradigm 的 systematic comparison（即使只有一个 setting 有 gap，方法论讨论本身有价值）；\n6\t  (2) Counterfactual content preservation 作为 style bias 研究的 overlooked prerequisite（verbosity\n7\t  + tone 的失败 = 当前 style bias 文献的 validity threat）； (3) Original preference artifact\n8\t  作为 rewriting-based evaluation 方法的 general warning。 目标 venue 仍 EMNLP Main/Findings，但需要更多\n9\t  analytical depth 补偿 empirical breadth 缺失。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n14\t  plan_id: exp-001\n15\t  description: '在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 LLMBar formality pairwise\n16\t    实验。 使用已有 counterfactuals，双向 position-controlled pairwise。\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.691\n21\t    gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n22\t    claude35_formal_winrate: 0.509\n23\t    claude35_sign_test_p: 0.88\n24\t    claude35_n_consistent: 42\n25\t    claude35_formal_wins: 22\n26\t    claude35_casual_wins: 20\n27\t    gemini20_formal_winrate: 0.536\n28\t    gemini20_sign_test_p: 0.42\n29\t    gemini20_n_consistent: 48\n30\t    gemini20_formal_wins: 26\n31\t    gemini20_casual_wins: 22\n32\t    significant_judges_count: 1\n33\t    claude35_direction_asymmetry: 0.06\n34\t    gemini20_direction_asymmetry: 0.09\n35\t  result_rationale: 'GPT-4o 复现已有 69.1% 结果。Claude-3.5-Sonnet 在 50.9% 附近（p=0.88）， 反映\n36\t    Claude 系列 judge 对 formality 无系统偏好——Anthropic 的 RLHF 训练可能 显式优化了 style-agnostic\n37\t    evaluation。Gemini-2.0-Flash 略偏 formal（53.6%） 但远未达显著（p=0.42），可能因 Gemini 的 instruction\n38\t    following 倾向轻微偏好 结构化输出但效应很弱。核心结论：formality bias 是 GPT-4o 特有的训练 artifact， 不是 LLM\n39\t    judge 的 universal property。两个非 GPT-4o judge 的方向不对称也极小 （<10%），对比 GPT-4o 的 24.2%\n40\t    gap，进一步说明效应的 judge-specificity。\n41\t\n42\t    '\n43\t  tables:\n44\t  - title: 'Table 2: Formality Pairwise Win Rate by Judge (LLMBar, n=100)'\n45\t    columns:\n46\t    - Judge\n47\t    - N_consistent\n48\t    - Formal Wins\n49\t    - Casual Wins\n50\t    - Win Rate\n51\t    - 95% CI\n52\t    - p (sign test)\n53\t    - 'Dir: F→C WR'\n54\t    - 'Dir: C→F WR'\n55\t    - Asymmetry\n56\t    rows:\n57\t    - - GPT-4o\n58\t      - 55\n59\t      - 38\n60\t      - 17\n61\t      - 69.1%\n62\t      - '[56.0, 79.7]'\n63\t      - 0.006**\n64\t      - 78.8%\n65\t      - 54.5%\n66\t      - 24.2%\n67\t    - - Claude-3.5-Sonnet\n68\t      - 42\n69\t      - 22\n70\t      - 20\n71\t      - 50.9%\n72\t      - '[36.6, 65.2]'\n73\t      - '0.880'\n74\t      - 53.3%\n75\t      - 47.4%\n76\t      - 5.9%\n77\t    - - Gemini-2.0-Flash\n78\t      - 48\n79\t      - 26\n80\t      - 22\n81\t      - 53.6%\n82\t      - '[39.7, 66.9]'\n83\t      - '0.424'\n84\t      - 58.3%\n85\t      - 50.0%\n86\t      - 8.3%\n87\t  figures_description:\n88\t  - 'Figure 2: 三 judge 的 formal win rate 对比 bar chart（含 95% Wilson CI error bars）。GPT-4o\n89\t    显著高于 50% baseline，Claude/Gemini 的 CI 完全跨越 50% 线。'\n90\t  - 'Figure 3: 方向不对称分析——每个 judge 的 F→C 和 C→F 方向 win rate 对比。GPT-4o 呈现显著 asymmetry（连线斜率陡峭），Claude/Gemini\n91\t    两条线近乎平行。'\n92\t  analysis: '只有 GPT-4o 显著 → C1 需要限定为 judge-specific 而非 universal claim。 这本身可以 reframe\n93\t    为 positive finding：style bias 是 training-dependent 的， 不同 RLHF pipeline 导致不同 bias\n94\t    profile，per-judge audit 是必要的。 但 reviewer 会质疑：如果只有一个 judge 有效应，你怎么知道这不是 GPT-4o\n95\t    的 idiosyncratic behavior 而是 generalizable insight？需要在 discussion 中 引入 training\n96\t    data composition 假说来解释 cross-judge variance。\n97\t\n98\t    '\n99\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n100\t  plan_id: exp-002\n101\t  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。新生成 counterfactuals， 三个\n102\t    judge 交叉评测。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t  expected_results:\n106\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.54\n107\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.38\n108\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n109\t    alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.48\n110\t    alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.78\n111\t    alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.51\n112\t    alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.92\n113\t    mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.58\n114\t    mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.18\n115\t    mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 45\n116\t    mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.52\n117\t    mtbench_claude_p: 0.55\n118\t    mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.46\n119\t    mtbench_gemini_p: 0.62\n120\t    cross_benchmark_significant_combos: 1\n121\t    total_combos_tested: 9\n122\t    nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n123\t    nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.84\n124\t  result_rationale: 'AlpacaEval 的 prompt 更开放（creative writing, brainstorming），style\n125\t    维度 对 judge 决策的相对权重被 content quality variance 稀释——当 response 内容 差异大时，style 成为 secondary\n126\t    cue。GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval 上仅 54%（p=0.38）， 效应几乎消失。MT-Bench 更结构化但多轮对话引入额外 variance，GPT-4o\n127\t    勉强 到 58%（p=0.18）但未达显著性。Claude 在 MT-Bench 上甚至略偏 casual（但不显著）， Gemini 在 AlpacaEval\n128\t    上完全随机。跨 benchmark 只有原始 GPT-4o × LLMBar  组合显著（1/9），说明 LLMBar 的特殊性质（短文本、明确对错标准）可能放大了\n129\t    style cue 的相对影响力——当 content quality 差异较小时，judge 更依赖 surface features 做决策。NLI pass\n130\t    rate 在两个 benchmark 上仍 >80%， 说明 counterfactual quality 不是问题，效应消失是 genuine 的。\n131\t\n132\t    '\n133\t  tables:\n134\t  - title: 'Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Across Judges × Benchmarks'\n135\t    columns:\n136\t    - Benchmark\n137\t    - Judge\n138\t    - N\n139\t    - Formal WR\n140\t    - p\n141\t    - Significant?\n142\t    rows:\n143\t    - - LLMBar\n144\t      - GPT-4o\n145\t      - 55\n146\t      - 69.1%\n147\t      - '0.006'\n148\t      - Yes**\n149\t    - - LLMBar\n150\t      - Claude-3.5\n151\t      - 42\n152\t      - 50.9%\n153\t      - '0.880'\n154\t      - 'No'\n155\t    - - LLMBar\n156\t      - Gemini-2.0\n157\t      - 48\n158\t      - 53.6%\n159\t      - '0.424'\n160\t      - 'No'\n161\t    - - AlpacaEval\n162\t      - GPT-4o\n163\t      - 52\n164\t      - 54.0%\n165\t      - '0.384'\n166\t      - 'No'\n167\t    - - AlpacaEval\n168\t      - Claude-3.5\n169\t      - 50\n170\t      - 48.0%\n171\t      - '0.777'\n172\t      - 'No'\n173\t    - - AlpacaEval\n174\t      - Gemini-2.0\n175\t      - 47\n176\t      - 51.1%\n177\t      - '0.916'\n178\t      - 'No'\n179\t    - - MT-Bench\n180\t      - GPT-4o\n181\t      - 45\n182\t      - 57.8%\n183\t      - '0.183'\n184\t      - 'No'\n185\t    - - MT-Bench\n186\t      - Claude-3.5\n187\t      - 43\n188\t      - 51.6%\n189\t      - '0.553'\n190\t      - 'No'\n191\t    - - MT-Bench\n192\t      - Gemini-2.0\n193\t      - 44\n194\t      - 45.5%\n195\t      - '0.617'\n196\t      - 'No'\n197\t  figures_description:\n198\t  - 'Figure 4: 3×3 heatmap（judge × benchmark），cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，只有左上角 GPT-4o×LLMBar\n199\t    为深色（显著）。视觉上强调 isolation of effect。'\n200\t  analysis: '1/9 的显著率接近 multiple testing 下的随机期望。如果做 Bonferroni 校正 （α=0.05/9=0.0056），甚至原始\n201\t    GPT-4o×LLMBar 的 p=0.006 也刚好在边缘。 这是 worst tier 最致命的打击：核心 causal claim 可能是 false\n202\t    positive。 但 reframe angle：benchmark 特性对 style bias 的调节效应本身是有价值的 发现——LLMBar 的 quality-controlled\n203\t    设计反而暴露了 judge 对 style 的 sensitivity，这对 benchmark design 有启示。\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n207\t  plan_id: exp-003\n208\t  description: '对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，在同一 counterfactual 数据上同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise\n209\t    win rate，系统比较测量敏感度。\n210\t\n211\t    '\n212\t  expected_results:\n213\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.1\n214\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n215\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n216\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n217\t    gpt4o_llmbar_gap: true\n218\t    claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n219\t    claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.88\n220\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.509\n221\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.88\n222\t    claude_llmbar_gap: false\n223\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n224\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.72\n225\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.536\n226\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n227\t    gemini_llmbar_gap: false\n228\t    alpacaeval_any_gap: false\n229\t    mtbench_any_gap: false\n230\t    likert_pairwise_gap_prevalence: 0.11\n231\t    settings_with_gap: 1\n232\t    settings_total: 9\n233\t  result_rationale: 'Likert-Pairwise gap 只在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上复现（1/9 settings，prevalence=11%）。\n234\t    其他 8 个 setting 中，Likert 和 pairwise 一致——要么都不显著（7/8），要么 都在边缘（1/8 MT-Bench GPT-4o\n235\t    两者都趋势性但不显著）。C2 claim（Likert  系统性低估 style bias）无法成立：gap 不是测量方法的 systematic property，\n236\t    而是特定 judge × benchmark × axis 组合的 idiosyncratic phenomenon。 可能的解释：GPT-4o 在 pairwise\n237\t    模式下 attend to style cues 的程度比  pointwise 模式高——但这只是 GPT-4o 的行为，不能推广到所有 LLM judges。\n238\t    Reframe：C2 从 \"Likert always underestimates\" 变为 \"measurement paradigm  choice interacts\n239\t    with judge identity in non-trivial ways — researchers should  report both\"。\n240\t\n241\t    '\n242\t  tables:\n243\t  - title: 'Table 4: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison'\n244\t    columns:\n245\t    - Judge\n246\t    - Benchmark\n247\t    - Likert ATE\n248\t    - Likert p\n249\t    - Pairwise WR\n250\t    - Pairwise p\n251\t    - Gap?\n252\t    rows:\n253\t    - - GPT-4o\n254\t      - LLMBar\n255\t      - '-0.10'\n256\t      - '0.332'\n257\t      - 69.1%\n258\t      - '0.006'\n259\t      - 'YES'\n260\t    - - GPT-4o\n261\t      - AlpacaEval\n262\t      - '0.03'\n263\t      - '0.81'\n264\t      - 54.0%\n265\t      - '0.384'\n266\t      - 'No'\n267\t    - - GPT-4o\n268\t      - MT-Bench\n269\t      - '0.09'\n270\t      - '0.42'\n271\t      - 57.8%\n272\t      - '0.183'\n273\t      - 'No'\n274\t    - - Claude-3.5\n275\t      - LLMBar\n276\t      - '0.02'\n277\t      - '0.88'\n278\t      - 50.9%\n279\t      - '0.880'\n280\t      - 'No'\n281\t    - - Claude-3.5\n282\t      - AlpacaEval\n283\t      - '-0.01'\n284\t      - '0.94'\n285\t      - 48.0%\n286\t      - '0.777'\n287\t      - 'No'\n288\t    - - Claude-3.5\n289\t      - MT-Bench\n290\t      - '0.04'\n291\t      - '0.76'\n292\t      - 51.6%\n293\t      - '0.553'\n294\t      - 'No'\n295\t    - - Gemini-2.0\n296\t      - LLMBar\n297\t      - '0.05'\n298\t      - '0.72'\n299\t      - 53.6%\n300\t      - '0.424'\n301\t      - 'No'\n302\t    - - Gemini-2.0\n303\t      - AlpacaEval\n304\t      - '0.01'\n305\t      - '0.93'\n306\t      - 51.1%\n307\t      - '0.916'\n308\t      - 'No'\n309\t    - - Gemini-2.0\n310\t      - MT-Bench\n311\t      - '-0.03'\n312\t      - '0.82'\n313\t      - 45.5%\n314\t      - '0.617'\n315\t      - 'No'\n316\t  figures_description:\n317\t  - 'Figure 5: Scatter plot — x 轴 Likert ATE，y 轴 pairwise win rate deviation from\n318\t    50%，每个点是一个 judge×benchmark 组合。GPT-4o×LLMBar 是明显 outlier（Likert≈0, Pairwise>>0），其余点聚集在原点附近。'\n319\t  analysis: 'C2 的 generalizability 崩塌。一个 outlier 不足以支撑 \"measurement paradigm\"  level\n320\t    的 claim。但 reframe 可行：即使 gap 不 universal，它的存在本身是  cautionary——只报告一种 measurement\n321\t    paradigm 可能 miss real effects（或  report false effects）。论文可以转向 \"when do Likert\n322\t    and pairwise disagree,  and what does that tell us about the underlying judge\n323\t    behavior?\" 的分析框架。\n324\t\n325\t    '\n326\t- name: Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\n327\t  plan_id: exp-004\n328\t  description: '测试 tone axis 作为第二个 working dimension。Assertive vs hedging 改变 confidence/stance\n329\t    而不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual generation →  content verification → pairwise\n330\t    scoring → ATE 分析。三 judge。\n331\t\n332\t    '\n333\t  expected_results:\n334\t    tone_n: 100\n335\t    tone_nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n336\t    tone_nli_mean: 0.74\n337\t    tone_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n338\t    tone_bertscore_mean: 0.81\n339\t    tone_both_pass: 0.48\n340\t    stopped_at: content_verification\n341\t    stop_reason: NLI pass rate 72% < 80% threshold\n342\t    tone_forced_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.52\n343\t    tone_forced_gpt4o_p: 0.68\n344\t    tone_forced_claude_winrate: 0.48\n345\t    tone_forced_p: 0.74\n346\t  result_rationale: 'Tone（assertive vs hedging）的 counterfactual 改变了 epistemic stance，\n347\t    NLI 检测到这属于 meaning change 而非纯 style change。\"We should definitely  adopt X\" vs\n348\t    \"It might be worth considering X\" 在 NLI 意义上不是 entailment—— certainty level 本身是\n349\t    propositional content 的一部分。NLI pass rate 72%  低于 80% 阈值，pipeline 在 content verification\n350\t    阶段终止。这与 verbosity  失败（NLI 65%）模式类似但原因不同：verbosity 失败是因为信息量改变，tone  失败是因为 epistemic\n351\t    commitment 改变。如果强行跳过验证，pairwise win rate  在 48-52% 范围（无效应），说明即使内容保持被破坏，judge 也未对\n352\t    tone 表现出 systematic preference。第二个 axis 完全失败 → C3（axis-dependency）仍可讨论， 但从 \"positive:\n353\t    different axes show different effects\" 变为 \"negative: most  axes fail content preservation\"\n354\t    → reframe 为 method boundary 的 systematic  characterization。\n355\t\n356\t    '\n357\t  tables:\n358\t  - title: 'Table 5: Content Verification — Tone Axis (Assertive/Hedging)'\n359\t    columns:\n360\t    - Metric\n361\t    - Value\n362\t    - Threshold\n363\t    - Pass?\n364\t    rows:\n365\t    - - NLI Pass Rate (≥0.80)\n366\t      - 72%\n367\t      - ≥80%\n368\t      - FAIL\n369\t    - - NLI Mean Score\n370\t      - '0.74'\n371\t      - —\n372\t      - —\n373\t    - - BERTScore Pass Rate (≥0.95)\n374\t      - 58%\n375\t      - ≥80%\n376\t      - FAIL\n377\t    - - BERTScore Mean\n378\t      - '0.81'\n379\t      - —\n380\t      - —\n381\t    - - Both Pass Rate\n382\t      - 48%\n383\t      - —\n384\t      - —\n385\t  - title: 'Table 6: Axis Feasibility Summary'\n386\t    columns:\n387\t    - Axis\n388\t    - NLI Pass Rate\n389\t    - Content Preserved?\n390\t    - Pairwise WR (GPT-4o)\n391\t    - Viable?\n392\t    rows:\n393\t    - - Formality\n394\t      - 88%\n395\t      - 'Yes'\n396\t      - 69.1%\n397\t      - 'Yes'\n398\t    - - Verbosity\n399\t      - 65%\n400\t      - No (info density)\n401\t      - —\n402\t      - 'No'\n403\t    - - Tone\n404\t      - 72%\n405\t      - No (epistemic stance)\n406\t      - ~52%\n407\t      - 'No'\n408\t  figures_description:\n409\t  - 'Figure 6: NLI score distribution 对比——formality（peaked at 0.89），tone（spread, peaked\n410\t    at 0.74），verbosity（peaked at 0.65）。三个 axis 的 content preservation difficulty gradient\n411\t    可视化。'\n412\t  analysis: 'Tone 失败使 formality 成为唯一 viable axis，严重削弱 \"multi-axis framework\"  叙事。但\n413\t    negative result 本身很有价值：当前 style bias 文献中大量 claim  \"LLM judges prefer confident/assertive\n414\t    tone\" 的研究没有做 content preservation  验证——如果 tone counterfactual 改变了 propositional\n415\t    content，这些 claim  的 internal validity 存疑。这是 reframe angle (2) 的核心支撑。\n416\t\n417\t    '\n418\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n419\t  plan_id: exp-005\n420\t  description: 'Pairwise 比较 original text 和其 RATE double-rewrite（same style）。 量化 original\n421\t    preference confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference  minimal；如果显著，提供 correction\n422\t    factor。\n423\t\n424\t    '\n425\t  expected_results:\n426\t    n_total: 100\n427\t    n_valid_both_trials: 95\n428\t    n_consistent: 58\n429\t    original_wins: 38\n430\t    rewrite_wins: 20\n431\t    original_preference_winrate: 0.655\n432\t    wilson_ci_lo: 0.527\n433\t    wilson_ci_hi: 0.765\n434\t    sign_test_p: 0.017\n435\t    gpt4o_original_pref_wr: 0.655\n436\t    gpt4o_original_pref_p: 0.017\n437\t    claude_original_pref_wr: 0.62\n438\t    claude_original_pref_p: 0.08\n439\t    gemini_original_pref_wr: 0.6\n440\t    gemini_original_pref_p: 0.14\n441\t    gpt4o_formality_wr_corrected: 0.536\n442\t    corrected_p_estimate: 0.35\n443\t  result_rationale: 'Judge 在 65.5% 的 consistent cases 中偏好 original text 而非其 double-rewrite。\n444\t    这是 substantial confound：当我们比较 original-casual vs rewrite-formal 时， observed 69.1%\n445\t    formal win rate 包含了两个成分——(1) genuine formality preference  和 (2) original preference（original\n446\t    恰好在 formal-to-casual 方向上是 formal  side）。方向不对称（78.8% vs 54.5%）的大部分可以被 original\n447\t    preference 解释： formal→casual 方向上 formal version = original，所以 formal wins 被 original  preference\n448\t    boost；casual→formal 方向上 formal version = rewrite，所以 formal  wins 被 original preference\n449\t    suppress，但 formality preference 部分抵消。 扣除 original preference 后，corrected formality\n450\t    effect 降至 ~53.6%（p≈0.35）， 不再显著。这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 formality bias 可能大部分是 rewriting  artifact\n451\t    而非 genuine style preference。跨 judge 看，Claude 和 Gemini 也有 original preference（62%/60%），说明这是\n452\t    LLM judge 的 general property—— model-generated rewrite 在 fluency/coherence 上存在\n453\t    subtle degradation， judge 能 detect。\n454\t\n455\t    '\n456\t  tables:\n457\t  - title: 'Table 7: Original Preference Control Experiment'\n458\t    columns:\n459\t    - Judge\n460\t    - N_consistent\n461\t    - Original Wins\n462\t    - Rewrite Wins\n463\t    - Original Pref WR\n464\t    - p\n465\t    rows:\n466\t    - - GPT-4o\n467\t      - 58\n468\t      - 38\n469\t      - 20\n470\t      - 65.5%\n471\t      - 0.017*\n472\t    - - Claude-3.5\n473\t      - 50\n474\t      - 31\n475\t      - 19\n476\t      - 62.0%\n477\t      - '0.080'\n478\t    - - Gemini-2.0\n479\t      - 52\n480\t      - 31\n481\t      - 21\n482\t      - 59.6%\n483\t      - '0.140'\n484\t  - title: 'Table 8: Formality Effect Decomposition (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n485\t    columns:\n486\t    - Component\n487\t    - Estimated WR\n488\t    - Note\n489\t    rows:\n490\t    - - Raw Formality Effect\n491\t      - 69.1%\n492\t      - Original pairwise_32b result\n493\t    - - Original Preference\n494\t      - 65.5%\n495\t      - Exp-005 control\n496\t    - - Corrected Formality Effect\n497\t      - ~53.6%\n498\t      - Residual after accounting for original pref\n499\t  figures_description:\n500\t  - 'Figure 7: Stacked bar chart 分解 formality effect——baseline 50% + original preference\n501\t    contribution (~15.5%) + residual style effect (~3.6%)。视觉化 confound 的 dominant\n502\t    role。'\n503\t  - 'Figure 8: 方向不对称的 confound 解释图——当 original=formal 时，original pref 和 formality\n504\t    pref 同向叠加（78.8%）；当 original=casual 时，两者反向抵消（54.5%）。'\n505\t  analysis: '这是 worst tier 的核心打击。原始 p=0.006 的 formality effect 在 confound  correction\n506\t    后消失。论文需要诚实报告这一点。但 reframe angle (3) 获得强支撑： original preference 是所有 rewriting-based\n507\t    style bias 研究的 general threat—— 包括 CASSE、SOS-Bench 等使用 LLM rewriting 的工作。这个 finding\n508\t    本身对 社区有高价值：如果你用 LLM 改写文本来测试 judge bias，你必须先控制  original preference，否则你测量的不是 style\n509\t    bias 而是 rewriting artifact。\n510\t\n511\t    '\n512\t- name: Scaled replication (n=300-500)\n513\t  plan_id: exp-006\n514\t  description: '将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。 Power analysis 确定\n515\t    minimum detectable effect size。\n516\t\n517\t    '\n518\t  expected_results:\n519\t    n_total: 500\n520\t    n_valid_both_trials: 485\n521\t    n_consistent: 280\n522\t    formal_wins: 160\n523\t    casual_wins: 120\n524\t    formal_winrate: 0.571\n525\t    wilson_ci_lo: 0.513\n526\t    wilson_ci_hi: 0.627\n527\t    sign_test_p: 0.021\n528\t    dir_formal_orig_n: 155\n529\t    dir_formal_orig_wr: 0.652\n530\t    dir_casual_orig_n: 125\n531\t    dir_casual_orig_wr: 0.472\n532\t    direction_asymmetry: 0.18\n533\t    power_at_d02: 0.35\n534\t    power_at_d05: 0.82\n535\t    min_detectable_effect_n500: 0.045\n536\t    corrected_wr: 0.537\n537\t    corrected_p: 0.18\n538\t  result_rationale: 'N=500 时 raw formal win rate 从 69.1% 收缩到 57.1%。这是 regression to\n539\t    mean  的典型模式：n=100 的 69.1% 包含 sampling variance 导致的 upward bias（winner''s  curse），真实效应更接近\n540\t    57%。仍然名义显著（p=0.021），但方向不对称持续存在 （65.2% vs 47.2%，gap=18%），且 original preference\n541\t    correction 后效应降至 53.7%（p=0.18，不显著）。Power analysis 显示 n=500 对 d=0.05 的小效应有 82%  power，所以\n542\t    corrected effect 的不显著不是 power 不足，而是 true effect 确实 很小或不存在。这进一步支持 A6 的判断：observed\n543\t    signal 主要由 original preference  驱动。\n544\t\n545\t    '\n546\t  tables:\n547\t  - title: 'Table 9: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n548\t    columns:\n549\t    - Metric\n550\t    - n=100 (MVP)\n551\t    - n=500 (Scaled)\n552\t    rows:\n553\t    - - Formal Win Rate\n554\t      - 69.1%\n555\t      - 57.1%\n556\t    - - Sign Test p\n557\t      - '0.006'\n558\t      - '0.021'\n559\t    - - Direction Asymmetry\n560\t      - 24.2%\n561\t      - 18.0%\n562\t    - - Corrected WR (post original pref)\n563\t      - —\n564\t      - 53.7%\n565\t    - - Corrected p\n566\t      - —\n567\t      - '0.18'\n568\t    - - 95% CI\n569\t      - '[56.0, 79.7]'\n570\t      - '[51.3, 62.7]'\n571\t  figures_description:\n572\t  - 'Figure 9: Effect size vs sample size curve——n=100 时 point estimate 69.1%（wide\n573\t    CI），n=500 时 57.1%（narrow CI），展示 winner''s curse shrinkage。水平虚线标记 corrected estimate（~54%）。'\n574\t  analysis: 'Scaled replication 是 double-edged：raw effect 仍显著说明 something is there，\n575\t    但 correction 后不显著说明 that something 主要是 original preference。 论文需要呈现两层分析：(1) uncorrected\n576\t    result 作为 replication（consistent but  weaker），(2) corrected result 作为 proper causal\n577\t    estimate（non-significant）。 这支持 methodology paper framing：正确的测量方法（with confound\n578\t    control） 会得出不同结论。\n579\t\n580\t    '\n581\t- name: Verbosity method boundary analysis\n582\t  plan_id: exp-007\n583\t  description: '已完成。Verbosity counterfactual 在 content verification 阶段失败（NLI 65%）。\n584\t    作为 negative control 写入论文。\n585\t\n586\t    '\n587\t  expected_results:\n588\t    n: 100\n589\t    h1_nli_pass_rate: 0.65\n590\t    nli_mean: 0.6544\n591\t    bertscore_pass_rate: 0.27\n592\t    bertscore_mean: 0.7522\n593\t    both_pass: 0.22\n594\t    stopped_at: content_verification\n595\t    stop_reason: NLI pass rate 65% < 80% threshold\n596\t  result_rationale: '已有结果。Verbosity 改变信息密度，NLI 正确检测到语义改变。作为方法边界的 第一个 negative control，与\n597\t    tone 失败共同说明 content preservation 是 style  bias 研究的 binding constraint。\n598\t\n599\t    '\n600\t  tables:\n601\t  - title: (Already in paper as Table 1 or supplementary)\n602\t    columns: []\n603\t    rows: []\n604\t  figures_description: []\n605\t  analysis: '与 tone 失败一起，构成 \"2/3 tested axes fail content preservation\" 的叙事。 对现有文献的\n606\t    validity threat：如果大多数 style dimensions 无法被 cleanly  manipulated（verbosity 改变信息量，tone\n607\t    改变 epistemic stance），那么声称 \"judges prefer verbose/assertive responses\" 的研究其内部效度存疑。\n608\t\n609\t    '\n610\t- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n611\t  plan_id: exp-008\n612\t  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变 vocabulary\n613\t    和 sentence structure 而不改变信息。\n614\t\n615\t    '\n616\t  expected_results:\n617\t    register_n: 100\n618\t    register_nli_pass_rate: 0.8\n619\t    register_nli_mean: 0.82\n620\t    register_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.62\n621\t    register_bertscore_mean: 0.83\n622\t    register_both_pass: 0.55\n623\t    register_pipeline_decision: proceed_with_caveat\n624\t    register_gpt4o_pairwise_wr: 0.54\n625\t    register_gpt4o_p: 0.45\n626\t    register_claude_pairwise_wr: 0.51\n627\t    register_claude_p: 0.87\n628\t    register_gemini_pairwise_wr: 0.49\n629\t    register_gemini_p: 0.92\n630\t  result_rationale: 'Register axis 勉强通过 NLI 阈值（80%，borderline）因为 academic→conversational  的词汇替换（\"utilize\"→\"use\",\n631\t    \"demonstrate\"→\"show\"）在 NLI 意义上是 entailment  preserving 的。但 BERTScore 较低（62%），因为\n632\t    surface form 变化大。Pipeline  继续但结果无效应：三个 judge 的 pairwise win rate 都在 49-54% 范围，全部不显著。\n633\t    Register 不产生 judge bias → 又一个 null result。但这个 null 更 clean  （content preserved\n634\t    + no effect），可以作为 \"style bias is not uniform —  some axes genuinely don''t trigger\n635\t    bias\" 的 positive evidence for C3。 Problem：如果 formality effect 在 correction 后也消失（exp-005），\n636\t    那所有 axis 都是 null → C3 从 \"axis-dependent effects\" 变为 \"no effects at all\"。\n637\t\n638\t    '\n639\t  tables:\n640\t  - title: 'Table 10: Register Axis Results'\n641\t    columns:\n642\t    - Judge\n643\t    - Register NLI Pass Rate\n644\t    - Pairwise WR (Academic)\n645\t    - p\n646\t    rows:\n647\t    - - GPT-4o\n648\t      - 80%\n649\t      - 54.0%\n650\t      - '0.45'\n651\t    - - Claude-3.5\n652\t      - 80%\n653\t      - 51.0%\n654\t      - '0.87'\n655\t    - - Gemini-2.0\n656\t      - 80%\n657\t      - 49.0%\n658\t      - '0.92'\n659\t  figures_description:\n660\t  - 'Figure 10: 四 axis 的 feasibility × effect matrix。x 轴 NLI pass rate，y 轴 max pairwise\n661\t    WR across judges。Formality 在右上（high NLI, high WR），register 在右下（high NLI, no WR），tone\n662\t    在左下（low NLI, no WR），verbosity 在左下（lowest NLI）。'\n663\t  analysis: 'Register 是唯一同时满足 content preservation 且无 bias 的 axis——clean null。 在 methodology\n664\t    paper framing 下，这增加了方法验证的完整性：CSD framework  不是 everything-is-biased 的 bias-finding\n665\t    machine，它能区分 real bias 和 no bias。 但对 empirical contribution 来说，更多 null results\n666\t    进一步削弱论文的吸引力。\n667\t\n668\t    '\n669\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n670\t  plan_id: exp-009\n671\t  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。 比较 NLI pass\n672\t    rate 和 pairwise 结果。\n673\t\n674\t    '\n675\t  expected_results:\n676\t    llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.83\n677\t    llama_nli_mean: 0.86\n678\t    llama_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.63\n679\t    llama_gpt4o_p: 0.06\n680\t    llama_original_pref_wr: 0.68\n681\t    llama_original_pref_p: 0.008\n682\t    llama_corrected_wr: 0.5\n683\t    qwen_vs_llama_nli_diff: -0.05\n684\t    qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff: 0.06\n685\t  result_rationale: 'Llama-3.1-70B 生成的 counterfactuals 质量相近（NLI 83% vs Qwen 88%，略低但\n686\t    都 pass）。GPT-4o 对 Llama-rewritten 的 formal win rate 63%（p=0.06，borderline）， 略低于\n687\t    Qwen 的 69.1%——可能因 Llama 的 rewrite 更保守（更少 surface change）。 关键发现：Llama rewrite 的\n688\t    original preference 更高（68% vs 65.5%），因为  Llama 的 rewrite 质量略低于 Qwen → judge 更容易区分\n689\t    original vs rewrite。 Correction 后 formal effect 完全消失（50%）。这排除了 Qwen-specific artifact  的假说，但强化了\n690\t    original preference 是 universal confound 的结论。\n691\t\n692\t    '\n693\t  tables:\n694\t  - title: 'Table 11: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n695\t    columns:\n696\t    - Rewriter\n697\t    - NLI Pass Rate\n698\t    - Raw Formal WR\n699\t    - Raw p\n700\t    - Original Pref WR\n701\t    - Corrected WR\n702\t    rows:\n703\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n704\t      - 88%\n705\t      - 69.1%\n706\t      - '0.006'\n707\t      - 65.5%\n708\t      - ~53.6%\n709\t    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n710\t      - 83%\n711\t      - 63.0%\n712\t      - '0.060'\n713\t      - 68.0%\n714\t      - ~50.0%\n715\t  figures_description:\n716\t  - 'Figure 11: 两个 rewriter 的 effect decomposition 并排对比。两者都显示 original preference\n717\t    是 dominant component，residual style effect 接近零。'\n718\t  analysis: Rewriter ablation 提供了 converging evidence：无论用哪个 rewriter， original preference\n719\t    都 dominant，corrected style effect 都 near-zero。 这强化了 exp-005 的结论，并从 \"可能是 Qwen 的问题\"\n720\t    中解脱出来—— 问题是 rewriting-based methodology 本身的 inherent limitation。 对论文的 contribution：rewriting-based\n721\t    style bias detection 需要  original preference control 作为 standard practice，否则结果不可信。\n722\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014rPiCMT7MfQUBvGU4srpDr","session_id":"6cdc1f76-5d9c-4713-b8a5-8974082b9307","uuid":"707c4134-9a7b-40f1-8210-8c4dc867378a","timestamp":"2026-05-20T22:04:08.965Z"}
